module gunbc.guarantee_stall.enrolment_commit_evidence_remains_caller_authored_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, AwaitsOneGrounding, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when, GroundingUndeclared }

// A STALL, NOT A DROP (DESIGN section 4b(2)), and it is typed rather than written in prose because
// the alternative was measured: the gap it names is currently disclosed in an annotation in
// gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine and exercised by one claim in
// test.claim.approve_ios_enrolment_machine_persist_order_witness. An annotation is not evidence a
// machine claim holds (DESIGN section 4c) and a claim answers a question, it does not enumerate the
// class. As a row, the obligation has an identity, a population a fold can count, and a trigger whose
// operative half is re-measurable.
//
// THE SUBJECT, STATED EXACTLY. `gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine` seals the two values a remote
// enrolment effect consumes — EnrolmentCommitProof and EnrolmentEffectAdmission, both sole_constructor
// and minted only inside `enrolment_persist` — so no module outside it can write "this call was
// admitted". What it cannot seal is the INPUT that makes the admitted arm reachable: `CasOutcome` in
// std.durable_compare_and_set is an ordinary coproduct, and `cas_decide` is a pure fold, so the only
// party able to produce a `CasCommitted` anywhere in this tree is the caller. A caller that authors one
// reaches the admitted arm without any store having held a byte.
//
// WHY NO FOLD CAN CLOSE THIS FROM HERE, which is the reason this is a stall and not a defect to fix in
// the same PR: every commit fact available to any fold in any module is caller-authored, so a check
// "did a commit really happen?" is the caller's assertion being read back to it. The authority that can
// produce a commit fact it did not also let callers invent is the durable store, which owns both the
// read and the write. That makes the grounding a change to std.durable_compare_and_set (and the store
// realizing it), not to this consumer — and DESIGN section 3c says a consumer names its own ceiling
// rather than silently authoring a second path beside the one it waits on.
//
// WHAT HOLDS MEANWHILE, named so the row is not read as "nothing is established": the ordering itself
// IS mechanical. Persisting and admitting are one operation, so there is no earlier permission to
// reorder or reuse; an effect is bound to the digest of the record it was persisted for; the digest
// compared against the state's render is the one side of the pair the caller cannot make agree with
// itself; and both sealed carriers refuse a foreign literal at compile time, measured by the keyed
// SoleConstructorViolation REDs. What survives a caller-authored commit is therefore "acted on a
// record that was never stored", not "posted without persisting".
//
// CEILING IS MechanicallyPreventable AND NOT HIGHER, stated rather than flattered: a store-minted
// sole_constructor `CasOutcome` makes forgery impossible for every module outside the sealing one,
// which is prevention by mechanism. It is not structural impossibility, because `enrolment_persist`
// would still take the store's word for which bytes its slot held — the seal removes the caller's
// ability to invent a commit, not the consumer's dependence on the store's own honesty.
data enrolment_commit_evidence_remains_caller_authored_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "an enrolment remote effect's commit evidence is established by the store rather than asserted by the caller: std.durable_compare_and_set's CasOutcome is unsealed and cas_decide is a pure fold, so a caller-authored CasCommitted reaches the admitted arm of gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine's enrolment_persist with no store involved",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
  blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding {
    grounding: GroundingUndeclared
  },
  // THE POPULATION IS THE ADMITTED-ARM SET REACHABLE THROUGH A CALLER-AUTHORED COMMIT — enumerated
  // from the module that declares them, not described. Every member is an arm or a verdict a forged
  // `CasCommitted` reaches; a member list that drifted from the model would show up as this row
  // claiming coverage it no longer has, which is why it is data and not prose.
  population: BoundedPopulation {
    members: [
      "gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine EnrolmentPersistVerdict's EnrolmentPersistedAndAdmitted arm: reachable from enrolment_persist on any CasCommitted branch, whichever party built it",
      "gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine EnrolmentCommitProof: minted by enrolment_persistence_standing's LocallyCommitted arm from the caller's own attempt bytes",
      "gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine EnrolmentEffectAdmission: minted on the same CasCommitted branch, so an admission exists with no store receipt behind it",
      "gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine enrolment_effect_admitted's Present arm: hands that admission out as a permission",
      "gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine enrolment_call_admitted's admitted answer, for each of SubmitEnrolmentPost, ForwardApnsToken and EnrolmentReadbackProbe: the remote call proceeds on a commit no store attested",
    ]
  },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "std.durable_compare_and_set mints CasOutcome only through the durable store that owns the slot, as a sole_constructor type, and gunbc.approve_ios_enrolment_machine's enrolment_persist takes that store receipt rather than a caller-authored outcome")
}
